From e27fbbb731f3282a5fea5d1dbe42482067b35ea8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cinemaONE <35371193+cinema-ONE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 23:13:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Follow the offset sequence a remux's 3d-plane
 tag names

MakeMKV writes the playlist's offset_sequence_id into a "3d-plane" tag
on each PG track. Use it, and keep "PG stream n follows sequence n" only
as a guess for files without the tag.

The guess fails whenever a disc numbers its sequences out of PG stream
order or a remux drops PG streams. The Hugo remux keeps three, tagged
2, 9 and 1, and the guess picked 0, 1 and 2: the second English track
followed sequence 1 instead of 9, 42% of its subtitle frames at a
different depth, up to 30 px. In one library, 136 of 165 tagged 3D
remuxes have a track whose tag differs from its PG stream index.

A tag value of 255 means the stream follows no sequence, so its depth
comes from the subtitle depth setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
